From 521949c0d23828a7e8d317037e81a66eacf4363c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:48:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: openacc backend

The behaviours, models and material properties of the generic-parallel
interfaces can be generated for OpenACC (`openacc` backend), as for
OpenMP:

- the points are processed by a `parallel loop` construct, on the device
  selected by the compiler and the OpenACC runtime (a GPU with
  nvc++ -acc=gpu, the cores of the host with nvc++ -acc=multicore). The
  statistics are merged by reductions and the computations are
  synchronous: the queue of the execution options is not used;
- the memory space of a library is deduced from the compilation macros
  (getOpenACCMemorySpace in MFront/GenericParallel/MemorySpace.hxx): the
  one of the computations offloaded by nvc++ with -acc=gpu, `host` with
  -acc=multicore only, `device` with the other compilers;
- the OpenACC runtime of nvc++ uses the CUDA driver without the CUDA
  runtime: the `device_stack_size` option sets the stack size through the
  driver, on the CUDA context of OpenACC
  (MFront/GenericParallel/OpenACCStackSize.hxx);
- the shared data are copied once per device in the memory of OpenACC
  (acc_malloc), which is accessible without unified or managed memory;
- the minimum reductions of OpenACC on long long and unsigned long long
  return 1 on NVIDIA GPUs with nvc++ 25.11: the index of the first failed
  point of the behaviours is reduced as a size_t, and the indices of the
  material properties as unsigned long when it has the size of unsigned
  long long.

TFEL_DEVICE_CODE, TFEL_STATIC_VARIABLE and getConstantObject treat
nvc++ -acc=gpu as nvc++ -mp=gpu: the device code is selected in the whole
translation unit.

Configurations openacc-nvhpc-gpu (nvc++ -acc=gpu -gpu=mem:unified) and
openacc-nvhpc-multicore (nvc++ -acc=multicore). With the separate and
managed memory modes, nvc++ 25.11 fails to compile the headers of TFEL for
OpenACC (the device code refers to an undefined global variable created
for an empty function object): the GPU configuration uses the unified
memory mode, which requires the heterogeneous memory management of the
driver or a hardware coherent platform. As with OpenMP, a program compiled
by nvc++ -acc=gpu which loads libraries compiled by other compilers must
be linked with libnvhpcmanaux.

Tests: the comparisons of the behaviours with the generic interface (with
their TDLS sub-tests) and the tests of the material properties, for both
configurations, as for openmp. On the GPU, the test of the material
properties lowers the stack size through the CUDA driver and checks that
an evaluation preserving it fails. test-no-runtime-checks.cxx takes the backend
as the other test of the material properties (MFRONT_GPMP_TEST_BACKEND,
openmp by default).

Documentation: interfaces of the behaviours and of the material
properties, release notes, shared data.
